  "observations": [
    "Each gate row is a large objective jump relative to its immediately previous solve; residual dimensions and visual observation count also increase. This is consistent with a visual/window update coinciding with the cost rise, but aggregate telemetry cannot attribute cost to visual, IMU, or marginalization-prior factors.",
    "The gate-frame aligned position error is only about 0.011-0.024 m in these runs. The next raw telemetry sample returns below 1.0 within 0.064-0.132 s, but each two-second follow-up still has additional samples above the threshold.",
      "The first flight-window position error above 0.30 m occurs 2.508-4.028 s after the quality telemetry stamp used for the gate pairing. These trajectories are short and the controller begins fail-closed landing at the gate, so they neither prove the gate is a false positive nor establish the threshold as predictive.",
    "All four crossing rows report termination_type=1 and iterations=9. Those raw solver fields are retained without assigning a termination cause.",
    "The targets are dispatched 0.769-1.512 wall seconds before the gate, while cost is already rising before dispatch. Timing alone does not attribute the cost rise to the target motion."
  ],
